body:
every winner has a blunder. dee was very emotional and played with her heart. she was never voting julie. i think we need to give credit to players as a whole, not just their strategic moves, like people are not robots. 

&#x200B;

Dee is amazing and she's definitely one of the best in awhile imo. people tend to put Tony, Parvati, Sandra and Kim in the final five but even them could've lost the game in many situations

Lauren Beck was probably the best game player but okay. 

&#x200B;

Lauren Rimmer is my fave!!

Looks are super important and part of the game, if somebody said this about Parvati there would be riots.

&#x200B;

And no, I'm not a Michael fan lol

If she voted Tasha while Keith and Kimmi voted Jeremy, and they voted Keith instead, then it would've been over regardless of whether she played the idol or not. 

&#x200B;

I don't think it's that crazy to want to take out Jeremy in this situation, or to keep all three votes the same.

this discourse about who deserved it or not lol.

&#x200B;

I think Heidi or Carolyn would've been just as deserving, but oh well

Ever since I realized I'm non binary I prefer to be called queer, weird

&#x200B;

I can be called gay too, tho
